            "result_text": "Done! I've saved the regex to `/app/regex.txt`.\n\nThe regex works as follows:\n\n- **`(?=.*IPv4_PATTERN)`** — Positive lookahead that confirms the line contains an IPv4 address\n- **`.*\\b(DATE_PATTERN)\\b`** — Greedily matches everything, then backtracks to capture a date with word boundaries on both sides\n- **`(?!.*DATE_PATTERN)`** — Negative lookahead ensures no other date exists after the captured date (making it the last one)\n\nThe IPv4 pattern validates each octet (0-255) without leading zeros, and the date pattern allows months 01-12 and days 01-29 across all months (as specified)."
